#: admin/config/index.php:123
msgid "GDPR consent mode"
msgstr ""

#: admin/config/index.php:125
msgid "When enabled, identifying analytics requires consent from the selected integration. Anonymous or cookieless settings can collect limited counts without identifiers. If the integration is missing, SlimStat collects limited counts only. Disabling this setting permits identifying tracking without a consent check. Review consent, retention and privacy disclosures for your site."
msgstr ""

#: admin/config/index.php:128
msgid "Consent plugin integration"
msgstr ""

#: admin/config/index.php:130
msgid "<strong>GDPR Compliance:</strong> Integrate with a Consent Management Platform (CMP) to ensure tracking only occurs with user consent.<br/><br/><strong>SlimStat Consent Banner:</strong> (Recommended) Use SlimStat's built-in banner with customizable messaging and server-side consent tracking.<br/><strong>Via WP Consent API:</strong> Integrates with CMPs supporting WordPress Consent API (Complianz, CookieYes, etc.). Server-side consent checking available for both modes."
msgstr ""

#: admin/config/index.php:132
msgid "Select a consent integration"
msgstr ""

#: admin/config/index.php:133
msgid "SlimStat Consent Banner (Recommended)"
msgstr ""

#: admin/config/index.php:134
